Installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for this Vite + React project.

## Changes Made

### Created:
- None (only modified existing files)

### Modified:
- **app/package.json** - Added `@vercel/analytics` version 2.0.1 to dependencies
- **app/package-lock.json** - Updated lockfile with analytics package and its dependencies
- **app/src/main.jsx** - Added Vercel Analytics injection following Vite-specific instructions

## Implementation Details

Following the official Vercel Web Analytics quickstart documentation (https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart), I implemented the Vite-specific integration method:

1. **Installed the package**: Used npm to install `@vercel/analytics@^2.0.1`
2. **Added analytics injection**: Modified `main.jsx` to import and call `inject()` from `@vercel/analytics`
   - Import statement: `import { inject } from '@vercel/analytics';`
   - Called `inject()` before rendering the React app
   - This is the recommended approach for Vite projects per the official documentation

## Verification

✅ Build completed successfully (`npm run build`)
✅ Linter ran without errors (`npm run lint`) - existing warnings are pre-existing and unrelated to this change
✅ Package lockfile properly updated to ensure consistent dependency resolution
✅ Code follows existing project patterns and conventions

## Notes

- The analytics will automatically start tracking page views once the application is deployed to Vercel
- No additional configuration is needed - the `inject()` function handles all setup
- The implementation is minimal and non-intrusive, preserving all existing code structure
- Analytics data will be visible in the Vercel dashboard after deployment
